<h1>Topics — where each pressure-test lives</h1>
<p class="lede">A wayfinding index only. The fourteen pressure-tests — thirteen across four layers, plus one cross-cutting fourteenth (register/care) — by their plain names, with links to where each is defined, debated, drawn, and measured. Nothing is claimed on this page that is not already on the pages it points to.</p>
<p>Throughout the record the tests carry short codes — <strong>M</strong> for the master condition, <strong>D1–D4</strong> the drivers, <strong>Y1–Y4</strong> the dynamics, <strong>S1–S4</strong> the symptoms, and <strong>R</strong> the cross-cutting register/care test promoted from dissent at Session 4k.</p>
<p class="companion-note">Every topic below is: defined in <a href="{{ '/docs/goals/' | url }}">Goals</a> · debated in <a href="{{ '/panel/session_2_pressure_tests/' | url }}">Session 2</a> · its arrows drawn in <a href="{{ '/docs/pressure_tests_causal_hypothesis/' | url }}">the causal hypothesis</a> · its status measured on <a href="{{ '/diagrams/' | url }}">Self-audit &amp; figures</a>.</p>
<p class="companion-note">Care entered the list late, and by promotion rather than design. Through <a href="{{ '/panel/session_2_pressure_tests/' | url }}">Session 2</a> it was carried only as a dissent — <a href="{{ '/docs/episode_unit/' | url }}">the repair-episode unit</a> named maintenance-shaped repair (care systems, mutual aid) as a structural blind spot left uncut ("the invisible load-bearing wall" — Le Guin, preserved in dissent), and Session 2 kept the objection on the record as D-005. At <strong>Session 4k</strong> that dissent was promoted to <strong>R</strong>, the fourteenth pressure-test: a cross-cutting, reflexive register that audits the list and its apparatus rather than sitting inside a layer. R is <em>drafted and untested</em> — it names the blind spot, it does not close it — and because it turns on a foreign vantage this closed build does not admit, it stays conclusively untested here. Naming a test is not yet accounting for it.</p>
<p class="companion-note">The master condition <strong>M</strong> is contested at the root, beyond the base-or-summit question (Q-002): <a href="{{ '/outputs/candidate_theories/' | url }}">Theory D in waiting</a> — Luhmann's differentiation rival — holds there may have been no single shared coherence to lose, and that the "vacuum" is how a functionally differentiated society feels to a centre-expecting observer. It is recorded, not built, and not ruled against A/B/C here; it is refuted if a genuinely shared, cross-system "why" can be shown to have existed and then measurably fractured.</p>
